    bounds: [135, 150, 1060, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Does learned attention add value?</strong></p>
  - elementId: answer-1-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [135, 185, 1060, 55]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p><strong>Yes.</strong> Positive attention value-add in 30/30 seeded runs. Modest but consistent: a stationary, near-uniform reweighting of neighbour pooling. The composite is real, unique, and consistent — but does not beat the single best island alpha.</p>
  - elementId: answer-2-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 270, 1160, 120]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$lightGray"
  - elementId: answer-2-num
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [80, 290, 40, 40]
    shapeName: ellipse
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: answer-2-num-text
    elementType: text
